idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  电闪雷鸣 | diàn shǎn léi míng | lightning flashes and thunder rumbles; severe thunderstorm
  雷厉风行 | léi lì fēng xíng | swift as thunder and speedy as wind; enforce strictly and vigorously
  吉光片羽 | jí guāng piàn yǔ | precious fragment of a mythological beast; rare artistic relics
  风驰电掣 | fēng chí diàn chè | swift as the wind and quick as lightning; traveling at immense speed

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  闪 | shǎn | flash; dodge; lightning | destello; esquivar; relampaguear | 门 | gate / door | 门 (double door leaf) | 人 (human slipping through door instantly) | 5 | 半包围结构 | Ideogrammic compound: a person (人) darting swiftly through an open doorway (门) like a flash of light. | A person (人) slipping swiftly through a doorway (门) like a momentary flicker of bright light. | Una persona (人) que cruza como un suspiro por el quicio de la puerta (门), veloz como un destello. | 214 | ANOR | 閃
  电 | diàn | electricity; lightning; telegram | electricidad; rayo; telégrafo | 田 / 申 | field / lightning flash | 雨 (ancient rain cloud) | 申 (zigzag lightning bolt streaking from sky) | 5 | 独体结构 | Ancient pictograph of an atmospheric lightning bolt zig-zagging downward from rainclouds to the earth. | A jagged lightning strike (电) zig-zagging across storm clouds to deliver electric energy. | Un rayo zigzagueante (电) que cruza el cielo nublado descargando una tremenda corriente eléctrica. | 51 | LWU | 電

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: A person darting through a doorway in a flash (闪) combined with atmospheric electricity (电) creates brilliant lightning (闪电).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Un destello fugaz (闪) junto a la descarga eléctrica del cielo (电) alumbra el potente relámpago (闪电).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: In ancient Chinese mythology, the Lightning Mother ('电母') wielded twin bronze mirrors that flashed across the skies to illuminate guilt and illuminate righteous retribution alongside the Thunder God ('雷公').
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Dipping 3rd tone followed by a falling 4th tone: shǎn diàn (214-51). Dip 'shǎn' smoothly into lower vocal pitch before delivering 'diàn' firmly downward.

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[4]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
    闪 | shǎn | flash; dodge | Has 门 (door) enclosing 人 (person)
    问 | wèn | ask; inquire | Has 门 enclosing 口 (mouth)
    电 | diàn | electricity; lightning | Five strokes with a curved right tail
    申 | shēn | express; extend | Has vertical stroke piercing through both top and bottom
  etymological_cognates[4]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
